<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">barbed-spike-plates</ansi> (blacksmithing recipe)

Riveted plates of forged barb-work, each spike hammered and angled
inward toward the plate's own center rather than out and away. Fitted to
a grip or a guard, the barbs face the clinch, not the swing -- built for
the moment something is already held and does not want to be. Ugly,
honest work, made for holding on.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Crafting ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Skill:</ansi>       blacksmithing (minimum 50)
  <ansi fg="yellow">Station:</ansi>     forge
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ingredients:</ansi> Steel Ingot (x2), Chain Link (x1), Coal Dust (x1)

